  "result": "Perfect! All 151 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement generation to the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/statements.js** - New customer statements module:\n   - `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` returns:\n     - `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` on success\n     - `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customers\n   - Filters invoices to include only:\n     - That customer (with ID normalization)\n     - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n     - issueDate on or before asOf date\n   - Each statement line includes:\n     - `number` - invoice number\n     - `issueDate` - when invoice was issued\n     - `dueDate` - when payment is due\n     - `total` - invoice total (from invoiceTotals)\n     - `due` - balance still owed (from balanceDue)\n   - Sorted by issueDate ascending\n   - `totalDue` is the sum of all due amounts\n\n2. **test/statements.test.js** - 12 comprehensive tests:\n   - Multiple invoices handling\n   - Date cutoff (asOf) filtering\n   - Status filtering (issued and partially_paid)\n   - Customer filtering\n   - Empty results for no matching invoices\n   - Unknown customer error\n   - ID normalization (case and whitespace)\n   - Correct due amount calculations\n   - Sorting by issueDate\n   - Total due summation\n   - All required fields validation\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- Uses existing invoiceTotals() and balanceDue() functions for accurate calculations\n- Normalizes customer IDs to handle mixed case and whitespace\n- Includes both issued and partially_paid invoices\n- Excludes paid invoices and draft invoices\n- Returns clean statement lines without internal invoice structure\n- Sorted by issue date for easy reading",
